/**
\var Filesystem::StringToType
\ingroup filesystem
\brief Maps the type names used in `filesystem.json` (`"TEXTURE"`, ...) to Filesystem::EAssetType values.
*/

/**
\struct Filesystem::SAssetData
\ingroup filesystem
\brief Everything the registry knows about one file: where it is, its asset path, name, extension, type and, once loaded, the loaded object.

Created for every file at startup. Declared at \src{include/Filesystem/FilesystemTypes.hpp,79,114}.

## How to use

Get one with Filesystem::GetAssetData(), read its fields, and pass it to `Filesystem::Importers::LoadFile<T>()` to load it. To add an asset made in code, create one with the default constructor, fill in `AssetPath`, `AssetName`, `AssetType` and `ObjectData`, and pass it to Filesystem::RegisterAssetData().

\genexopen{modules/AssetsAndMemory.cpp,Asset data}
\snippet modules/AssetsAndMemory.cpp asset_data
\endex
*/

/**
\var Filesystem::SAssetData::AssetFilePathRaw
\brief Full path of the file on disk. Empty for assets made in code.
\var Filesystem::SAssetData::AssetPath
\brief The asset path: relative to `Resources/`, without the extension, e.g. `Images\Player`. This is the registry key.
\var Filesystem::SAssetData::AssetName
\brief The file name without folder or extension, e.g. `Player`.
\var Filesystem::SAssetData::AssetExtension
\brief The file's extension including the dot, e.g. `.png`.
\var Filesystem::SAssetData::AssetType
\brief The asset type from `filesystem.json`.
\var Filesystem::SAssetData::ObjectData
\brief The loaded object, or empty until the asset is first loaded with `LoadFile`.
*/

/**
\struct Filesystem::SSoftAssetPath
\ingroup filesystem
\brief A reference to an asset by its path. Cheap to copy and store in components; nothing is loaded until you ask.

Converts implicitly from a string, a loaded asset, or an Filesystem::SAssetData, and back to `std::string`. `GetAssetData()` looks the path up in the registry. Declared at \src{include/Filesystem/FilesystemTypes.hpp,116,145}. Registered with flecs, so the Entity Debugger shows it as a drop-down of every asset.

\genexopen{modules/AssetsAndMemory.cpp,Register runtime}
\snippet modules/AssetsAndMemory.cpp register_runtime
\endex
*/

/**
\struct Filesystem::STypedSoftAssetPath
\ingroup filesystem
\brief An Filesystem::SSoftAssetPath that also states which asset type it points to.

The Entity Debugger uses the type to list only matching assets. Graphics::SSprite stores its texture this way. Constructing one from an Filesystem::SAssetData of a different type terminates the program (\src{include/Filesystem/FilesystemTypes.hpp,153,159}). Declared at \src{include/Filesystem/FilesystemTypes.hpp,147,166}.
*/

